msgid "`alloc`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:382
msgid ""
"Passes the collector, but no device-side allocator is wired up yet. Link-"
"time error today."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:413
msgid ""
"If the collector encounters a call into a forbidden crate, it reports a "
"compile-time error rather than generating broken PTX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:420
msgid ""
"The device code collector: starting from #[kernel] entry points, the "
"compiler walks the call graph to discover all reachable device functions, "
"then filters each callee against the allowed-crate list (local crate, "
"cuda_device, core). The output is a PTX module with .entry and .func "
"directives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:426
msgid "`no_std` and panic behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:428
msgid ""
"Device code runs in an implicit `#![no_std]` environment. You do not need to "
"add this attribute yourself -- the compiler backend handles it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:431
msgid ""
"**Panic behavior:** all unwind paths in MIR are treated as unreachable. If a "
"panic actually triggers at runtime (e.g., an array bounds check fails), the "
"GPU executes a **trap instruction**, which causes the host to receive "
"`CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_INSTRUCTION`. This is semantically equivalent to "
"`panic=abort` but does not require any special compiler flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:437
msgid "In practice this means:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:439
msgid "`unwrap()` and `expect()` work but will trap the GPU on `None`/`Err`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:440
msgid "`assert!` and `debug_assert!` work but trap on failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:441
msgid ""
"`panic!(\"message\")` compiles, and so does `panic!(\"{}\", value)`. The "
"panic path lowers to a trap and the **message is discarded**: there is no "
"panic runtime to print it, and the statements that would have built it are "
"dead once the call is dropped. Reach for `gpu_printf!` before the check when "
"you need to see the values, or `gpu_assert!` for an explicit check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernels-and-device-functions.md:448
msgid ""
"The [Error Handling and Debugging](error-handling-and-debugging.md) chapter "
"covers `gpu_printf!`, `gpu_assert!`, and `cargo oxide debug` for diagnosing "
"kernel failures."
msgstr ""
